   {
    "id": "05f26c6b-5ea0-419c-8da9-ad37bacf5a27",
    "kind": "section",
    "label": "1",
    "heading": "Short title and extent",
    "ordinal": 0,
    "first_page": 2,
    "preview": "(1) This Act may be called the Usurious Loans Act, 1918. (2) It extends to the whole of Pakistan.] (3) The 3[Provincial Government] may, by notification in the 4[official Gazette], direct that it shall not apply to any area, class of persons, or class of transactions which it may specify in its noti…",
    "group": null,
    "citation": "Usurious Loans Act, 1918, s. 1",
    "survives_repeal": false
   },
   {
    "id": "9b763bb2-592d-4410-bfb4-2b815bacc67e",
    "kind": "section",
    "label": "2",
    "heading": "Definitions",
    "ordinal": 4,
    "first_page": 2,
    "preview": "In this Act, unless there is anything repugnant in the subject or context,___ (1) “Interest” means rate of interest and includes the return to be made over and above what was actually lent, whether the same is charged or sought to be recovered specifically by way of interest, or otherwise. (2) “Loan…",
    "group": null,
    "citation": "Usurious Loans Act, 1918, s. 2",
    "survives_repeal": false
   },
   {
    "id": "f46c9cbf-d499-4623-9080-84544b465059",
    "kind": "section",
    "label": "3",
    "heading": "Re-opening of transactions",
    "ordinal": 11,
    "first_page": 3,
    "preview": "(1) Notwithstanding anything in the Usury Laws Repeal Act, 1855 (XXVIII of 1855), where, in any suit to which this Act applies, whether heard ex- parte or otherwise, the Court has reason to believe,___ (a) that the interest is excessive ; and (b) that the transaction was, as between the parties ther…",
    "group": null,
    "citation": "Usurious Loans Act, 1918, s. 3",
    "survives_repeal": false
   },
   {
    "id": "91574ef9-2529-4a61-91f0-e07c11ba296b",
    "kind": "section",
    "label": "4",
    "heading": "Insolvency proceedings",
    "ordinal": 30,
    "first_page": 4,
    "preview": "On any application relating to the admission or amount of a proof of a loan in any insolvency proceedings, the Court may exercise the like powers as may be exercised under section 3 by a Court in a suit to which this Act applies. ___________ Date: 11-09-2024",
    "group": null,
    "citation": "Usurious Loans Act, 1918, s. 4",
    "survives_repeal": false
   }
  ],
  "total": 4,
  "next_cursor": null
 },
